## 🔄 Bulk File Operations

### Upload Multiple Files
```bash
# Upload multiple recordings
for file in *.mp3; do
  # Create recording
  RECORDING_ID=$(curl -X POST https://app.knittt.com/api/recordings \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d "{\"name\": \"${file%.*}\", \"type\": \"upload\"}" \
    | jq -r '.id')
  
  # Upload file
  curl -X POST "https://app.knittt.com/api/recordings/${RECORDING_ID}/upload" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT" \
    -F "audio=@${file}"
    
  echo "Uploaded: $file as Recording ID: $RECORDING_ID"
done
```

### Bulk Deploy Uploaded Files
```bash
# Deploy multiple uploaded recordings to Asterisk
curl -X POST https://app.knittt.com/api/recordings/bulk/deploy-to-asterisk \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"recordingIds": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9]}'
```

